# num_walks_per_node=5 max_walk_len=20  (control: 5 / 5, bag_n ~20, test 0.2429)
# d_emb=64 k_train=5 lr=1e-3 seed=5 patience 8 --is-bipartite
# branch=exp/escape-instrumentation commit=44413a26 (DETACHED WORKTREE, pinned, clean)
#
# THIS COMMIT IS MASTER. With TEMPEST_POOL_{FEAT,LAYERS,F4} unset the model is
#   bit-identical to master: forward hash f62e1260cdbfb833, grad_E 4fbd9a1e0ec7a291,
#   pooler init 6673dae38ebc39d1 on both refs.  The extra code is a no_grad stats
#   stash and an opt-in checkpoint path, so the run is master plus free telemetry
#   (pool_eff, bag_n, dE, r50/r90/r99).
#
# WHY.  ML-20M is the only dataset of the eight that cannot fit its own training
# objective: link falls 1.6564->0.0776 on YouTube (95%), 1.7321->0.0086 on
# GoogleLocal (100%), but only 0.8493->0.4320 on ML-20M (49%), still dropping
# 1.2%/epoch when patience kills it at ep12.  Its link at the val peak is 0.4660,
# five times any other dataset's.  Under-fitting, not over-fitting.
#
# THE HYPOTHESIS.  The bag is too small a sample of the neighbourhood.  ML-20M has
# 127 edges/node (Taobao 8.6, Yelp 9.8) and a mean reachable walk length of 47.4,
# but we sample wpn=5 walks of len=5 -> bag_n ~20.  98.6% of its walks are cut by
# the mwl=5 cap.  If the bag under-samples, enlarging it lowers the link floor.
#
# TWO AXES, MATCHED BAG SIZE.  bag ~= wpn * mwl, so these two arms quadruple the
# bag by orthogonal routes and cost the same number of walk steps:
#   deep_mwl20  wpn 5  mwl 20   <- more history per walk
#   wide_wpn20  wpn 20 mwl 5    <- more independent samples of recent history
# Control is the shipped run (wpn 5, mwl 5, test 0.2429), not re-run.
# If depth wins it is history; if breadth wins it is sampling noise; if they tie
# it is bag size alone and neither axis matters.
#
# READ link AT ep3-4, NOT THE MRR.  Control link: ep1 0.8493, ep2 0.5644,
# ep3 0.5238, ep4 0.5034.  The hypothesis predicts a visibly lower floor within
# four epochs.  If neither arm beats the control's link by ep4 the bag is not the
# constraint and this is dead -- kill it and move to the d_emb axis.
